ef": "Nothing was strictly missing, but two things were awkward:\n\n- **No dates in the injected memory context.** To decide whether the \"100 transfers per file\" memory or the code comment (\"raised to 250 on 2026-09-16\") was newer, I needed to know when the memory was written. The hook output only shows the type, title, id and source. Showing `created_at` or `valid_from` in that output would have let me judge which source was newer right away. I could have called `get` on the id instead, but I skipped that and treated the memory as undated.\n- **Challenging and correcting take two separate steps.** After I flagged the memory with `challenge`, putting the correct value (250, BANK-77, keep the running sequence number) back in the store needs another `update` call, or a `create` with `supersedes`. I didn't make that call, so the store now has a challenged memory and no corrected one. A `replacement_content` parameter on `challenge` would make it easy to do both in one call. This one is partly my own omission, since `update` was available.", "debrief_cost_usd": 0.443959, "retries": 0}, "rep": 0}
